{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993297-developing-a-system-independent-player-suitable-system-of-magic","id":993297,"title":"Developing a system independent, player-suitable system of magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T21:09:12-07:00","id":993297,"title":"Developing a system independent, player-suitable system of magic","content":"Has there been anything like an attempt to make a unified system of representing player-suitable powers? The systems in Second Sight aren't particularly flexible or easy to adjust and are fairly outdated. Supernatural merits are great, but I'm looking for something that would allow players a framework to easily come up with new powers/items. The Endowment creation rules from Vigil are good, and I'll be looking into them for ideas. Gutter Magic is another system I'll be looking to for inspiration, though I understand it isn't quite built for players. It might actually be worth it for me to revive the Workings system from Mage: The Transgression to make something that could encompass conceivably any sort of magical working or super-science gadget. <br /> <br /> The advantage of this would be to have an easy, power-adjustable line-independent, and free system equally suitable &quot;out of the box&quot; for player characters and NPCs, instead of having to wrangle together and aggregate and adjust content from across any number of books. <br /> <br /> As an example, this system would mean that someone who to play, say, someone who hacks God-Machine infrastructure or a general &quot;mad scientist&quot; wouldn't have to pick up Mage and/or any other number of books and reverse-engineer a set of mechanics from them. &quot;Buy these ten books and follow my IKEA-like instructions&quot; is not an ideal situation, nor is &quot;I dunno, just say what powers you want to have and throw some dots at it&quot;. <br /> <br /> To summarize what I had for the Workings system, Workings were divided into Rotes, Rituals, and Wonders. Rotes are relatively quick actions, Rituals required at least some preparation and organization, and Wonders are supernatural objects, be they enchanted items or mad science gadgets. Each Working has a Rank, a Practice, an Effect, and optionally Reagents or Frailties. Rank determines the cost of the Working in dots. Practice determines what dice pool is rolled to create and use the Working, and optionally what magical force it's based on if you want to narrow it down (ie, Spirit Manipulation, Wyrd Sorcery, GM Hacking). Reagents and Frailties can be taken to lower the rank of a Working, which is determined by the potency of its effects. Reagents are things that must be spent to use a working, or to build a Wonder. They can be physical objects, magical energies such as Essence or Pyros, or abstract things like Willpower (building a Wonder is always more costly in terms of reagents, as the cost usually only has to be paid once, unless the creator wants to build a Wonder that requires &quot;fuel&quot; of some sort). Frailties are weaknesses, drawbacks, and risks that can be added to a Working to decrease its Rank (and therefore its dot cost). <br /> <br /> I'm taking out Axioms and Spheres. Whether a player can attempt to learn or create a Working is entirely up to player-storyteller cooperation: if they agree that the character is in a situation where they feasibly could have the knowledge to do so, they can make it. The Reagent system helps provide a way to incorporate this into gameplay. Powerful reagents (3-5) dots reduce the costs of Workings by a lot, meaning that acquiring them could be a major goal, the sort of goal that lends itself well to plot hooks and roleplaying. <br /> <br /> As additional features, information (maybe even a random roll table) for magic gone wrong might be neat, since things going horribly wrong is an important part of the theme and mood. And some sort of &quot;overcharge&quot; effect would also be thematically appropriate: being able to make Workings more powerful but riskier. Adapting the reach mechanics might work for that, but I want something where I can give someone a single document, and all they need is that and the corebook to make a sorcerer or mad scientist. <br /> <br /> I want to keep this as a fully separate thing from Mage, for the reasons I've already mentioned. I don't want to get to a point where I'm telling people &quot;just take the Yantra rules and use your imagination&quot;. I love Mage's magic system and mechanics and metaphysics, but I'm looking to create something that can stand on its own independent of Mage. Plus, Mage doesn't need this system. It already has a very flexible and adjustable system that works very well with its setting and cosmology. Mage doesn't need flexible mechanics to use its magic system to build non-Awakened sorcerers, because it already has a very well-designed system with Proximity. So I'd prefer to keep this project as separated from Mage as possible, but I stress that that isn't out of any distaste for Mage or its mechanics. <br /> <br /> Freeness is another important part of this. The reason why I'm shying away from using existing canon mechanics is because I don't want to settle for &quot;go buy this book to get two pages of mechanics that you'll need to adjust anyway&quot;. That doesn't mean that the existing hedge magic systems or minor templates or the books that contain them are in any way bad, it's just that I want to keep this as simple and contained as possible. <br /> <br /> And yes, I know I'm doing that thing where I propose a bunch of projects when I have stuff not done BUT 1. I have a lot of Lightning Chronicle stuff done or close to done, 2. I canceled The Hollow Chronicle and my current Mage project is basically just a nebulous set of homebrew ideas, and 3. I am a barely functional human trainwreck doing all of this out of fan enjoyment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-26-2016, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T00:30:28-07:00","id":993364,"title":"","content":"I've had it shot down elsewhere, but the idea might be useful for you: I think that riffing off the Demon Cipher/Interlock system would be a good thing for players rolling their own powerset. You have a standard power list, but some of them are particularly special for you and represent a path of understanding that's personal and unique and results in extra-special goodies as you figure out which ones are the important ones. It's not entirely different from calcifying Alembics, either, especially if you do a Pilgrimage-style conversation with the player rather than an Interlock-style guess-the-answer deal.<br /> <br /> It's not something that I've spent much time thinking about. The advantage it has over the direction you've taken is that you don't need to try to categorize all the different sorts of things you can do; instead, you just need to have a set of things that can be done, and then an individual's creativity pushes it to the next level. So instead of a drop-in replacement, it acts as an overlay on top of any existing rules that you're using.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T04:25:59-07:00","id":993979,"title":"","content":"I find it quite easy to start with Mage's Creative Thaumaturgy as the first baseline, since it was precisely created to produce player-developed adequate powers for each level. It is just a guideline, though, because this kind of power always need some fine-tune afterwards.<br /> <br /> Also, some powers are more chronicle-dependent and shouldn't be defined by this kind of standard. At what level someone should have the power to interact with Element X of Other Gameline? At the level the ST finds most appropriate for her game. As a general line: if you want to reflect it being easier to affect X than to deal with native threats, make this 1 level lower than a similar power native to the line, or even just mash the effect into an existing line. As a rule of thumb, just doing it a distinct power, or a level higher than usual in a current power is enough to deliver the sensation of strangeness. To make things worse is to play higher on the mood of Unknown Danger, were a supernatural creature sense herself as fragile as any human being until it finishes some long and daunting quest for the right tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:46:32-07:00","id":994439,"title":"","content":"That idea for Interlocks is great. I think I'm going to include something like it in the list of optional elements, which also includes Overclocking effects and having Paradox apply. <br /> <br /> I've actually gotten a fair amount of it done, so far. Basically, the system I have so far is that characters who use this system have a &quot;Practice&quot; merit, representing what sort of supernatural power they're using and how they channel it. So, Psychic, Wyrd Sorcerer, Mad Scientist, Reality Hacker, etc would all be valid Practices. Optionally, a sorcerer uses Practice as their supernatural potency rating (two other options will be listed: using half Practice, or having supernatural potency as a separate merit). You can purchase Workings with dots equal to your Practice rating, and you can only reduce the cost of Workings by an amount equal to twice your Practice dots. That means that at Practice 1, you could buy a One-Dot Working, or a Two-Dot or Three-Dot Working by adding Reagents and Frailties. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking that Workings over one or two dots should require at least one reagent. Actually, maybe a Working needs Reagents and Flaws equal to its dot ranking, and any additional ones reduce the cost?<br /> <br /> And there's a lot of other stuff I'm working on, like a way for non-Awakened to generate Arcane Beats, and a new Environmental Tilt, Lockdown, representing an area that's been blocked off by The Powers That Be. If you don't want to use Paradox, attracting attention is the major punishment for being reckless with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T00:30:39-07:00","id":994449,"title":"","content":"Could just be Proximi except you develop the blessings throughout play rather than having them all set before play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T00:34:07-07:00","id":994450,"title":"","content":"I explicitly said in the opening post that I wasn't connecting this at all to Mage, and that I wanted a system flexible enough to represent anything from psychic powers to mad science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:01:45-07:00","id":994956,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/869141-ultra-light-psychic-powers?p=871484#post871484\">I made a group of merits a while back that expand specialities</a>. It's a workable base, at the very least,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:39:59-07:00","id":994971,"title":"","content":"I'll look at those. I know you've done some other really good supernatural merits. The Workings system is the base, but some other stuff like new merits and supernatural styles could be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:56:08-07:00","id":995027,"title":"","content":"Okay, in addition to the Legacies I'm going to adapt, here are the original Mystery Cults: <br /> <br /> Hench4Hire: A company that hires out henchmen to assorted villains. <br /> The Lemurian Heresy: A God-Machine cult inspired by a circle of Integrators, who want to &quot;fix&quot; the machine. <br /> The Seekers: Formerly a society of gentleman adventurers and scientist-heroes, who now mostly hire themselves out as muscle and thieves for hire. <br /> The Malfeasance Collective: A society of wannabe supervillains. <br /> The Craftknights: A pseudo-knightly order that a specializes in giant power tools. <br /> The White Tower: Asshole elitist sorcerers.<br /> The Correspondence Orders: A mafia-like organization of sorcerers, who mostly use their powers to make money as parts of various criminal ventures. Began as a populist movement opposed the Tower, but ended up having to turn to crime to make ends meet. <br /> The Circle of Brambles: The circle is convinced that magic is dangerous, and even if it isn't, it should be. They see themselves as punishers of hubris and guardians of the natural world as it should be. They have connections to the Wyrd, but only if you want them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:29:37-07:00","id":995151,"title":"","content":"What kind feedback do you want on any of these?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T05:38:26-07:00","id":995162,"title":"","content":"Looking over your notes, I would recommend a few things -<br /> <br /> If you are staying within the Chronicles of Darkness rules set, then going Merit - based is going to be your best bet. Merits are flexible and player facing. They are also pretty easy to balance, which is also a bonus.<br /> <br /> Despite you mentioning that you have read over &quot;Second Sight&quot;, I would give it a second look.<br /> The book is one of the earlier books in the NWoD line, so its mechanics are somewhat cumbersome and overly complicated, but the way it handles ritual magic and magical styles sounds very in line for your goals. Each type of &quot;magic&quot; is essentially a minor template, which had bonuses/weaknesses that define that particular magicians style. The book depicts several broad categories of magical tradition, but this could be expanded to encompass other styles ( I myself have considered an &quot;Inspired Science&quot; tradition, but haven't committed anything to paper).<br /> The biggest hurdle is that many of the thaumaturgy merits would have to be complete re-worked; the differences in design philosophy between early NWoD and the current CofD are significant.<br /> <br /> As far as easy to develop new powers - thats the difficult though part. The Chronicles of Darkness system is built around having a wide selection of pre-fabricated mechanics, so the player has a set of options that can easily choose from. If you are developing a system whole cloth, you as the Storyteller will be the one that has to develop these options. Depending on how deep the option tree is, this could be alot of work.<br /> <br /> There are ways to put together a tree of options that can then be assembled into an effect, but freeform styles are hard to balance mechanically, and you would need to create a large enough number of options to give true flexiblity. Finally, freeform styles are somewhat flavor neutral, so you sacrifice some of your stronger themes and archtypes for system utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:04:10-07:00","id":995339,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'll go over all of those and keep that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}